    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 00 · ORCHESTRATOR — start here\nSingle entry point for the whole CRM Hygiene & Deduplication system.\n\n**Before your first run**\n1. Import workflows 10 / 20 / 30 / 40 / 99 as well.\n2. Open each `Execute Workflow` node here and pick the real sub-workflow.\n3. Set the HubSpot + Slack credentials once per workflow.\n4. Create the 5 custom HubSpot properties (see SETUP-GUIDE.md).\n\n**`dryRun` ships as TRUE.** Nothing is written to HubSpot until you\nflip it to false in ⚙️ Global Config. Always do one dry run first.",
        "height": 250,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "d630fece-de5b-4f23-835c-3776d5380f4d",
      "name": "note-0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### ⚙️ Global Config\nEvery tunable in the system lives here and is passed down to all\nsub-workflows — never hard-code values inside the sub-workflows.\n\n`autoMergeThreshold 95` = only an exact normalised-email (or exact\ndomain) match merges without a human.\n`reviewThreshold 72` = goes to Slack for approval.\n`logThreshold 55` = reported only, never touched.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "c46d0c3e-f36b-4ded-b5a9-0647614c0643",
      "name": "note-1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        288,
        688
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Why jobs run one at a time\nBatch size 1 keeps you inside HubSpot's rate limit (100 req / 10s on a\nprivate app) and makes the execution log readable when a client asks\n\"what did it do to my database?\".\n\nHygiene always runs before dedup — normalising emails and domains\nfirst is what makes the duplicate scoring accurate.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "9f9332a1-237f-41d6-a06a-3173ed214d17",
      "name": "note-2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        736,
        752
      ]
    }
